# Sponsors — update the project immediately

When the operator reports a new BetterDesk supporter (Buy Me a Coffee, GitHub Sponsors, honorary, or similar):

1. **Update [`SPONSORS.md`](SPONSORS.md) in the same session** — do not defer or wait for a release.
2. **Update [`web-nodejs/config/supporters.json`](web-nodejs/config/supporters.json)** in the same session so the console Help panel matches `SPONSORS.md` (honorary / individuals / links). Add logo files under `web-nodejs/public/img/supporters/` when needed.
3. Place the entry in the correct section:
 - **Individual Backers** — one-time BMC / small personal donations (same pattern as existing entries).
 - **Honorary Supporters** — significant non-monetary or special recognition (also update README badge when applicable).
 - GitHub Sponsors **Bronze+** — follow tier perks in `SPONSORS.md` (logo/README as required).
4. Use the supporter’s preferred public name; link GitHub when known. Mention relevant issues only if they contributed a useful report.
5. Bump `*Last updated:*` at the bottom of `SPONSORS.md`.
6. **Commit and push to `main`** (or the branch the operator names) so the list is public promptly — sponsors are not “dev-only” docs.
7. Do **not** imply Commercial Grant for Buy Me a Coffee or $5/$15 GitHub tiers (see [`docs/COMMERCIAL-GRANT.md`](docs/COMMERCIAL-GRANT.md)).

## Checklist

- [ ] Entry added under the right heading in `SPONSORS.md`
- [ ] Matching entry/links updated in `web-nodejs/config/supporters.json`
- [ ] `Last updated` date refreshed
- [ ] Committed and pushed to the public default/`main` path the operator requested
